# Shared Worktree Coordination

- Treat the files currently on disk as the source of truth because several sessions may edit this project concurrently.
- Start by checking `git status --short` and reading every file you plan to modify.
- Re-read each target file immediately before editing; do not rely only on cached context or pasted snapshots.
- Preserve unrelated staged, unstaged, and untracked work.
- Merge into the current file contents if another session changed them; never overwrite or revert newer work.
- Inspect the final diff and stage only files belonging to the current task.
